aktar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2019-03-07T06:32:19Z","updated_at":"2019-03-07T06:32:19Z","body":"@jenniferfell yes, that's accurate except that item `1` can't be solved independently. It needs an answer to either `2` or `3`, perhaps both.\r\n\r\n@wKoza thank you for that information. That's helpful, but it would be good to have some kind of evidence and reasoning before we recommend/require that Angular framework contributors install an old version of the Java SDK. As far as I can tell from [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Java_version_history), Oracle put out the last free commercial update to Java 8 LTS in January 2019. It looks like they may update Java 8 for personal use for free until December 2020. Then it is EOL in 2025. \r\n\r\nNote that Java 9 and 10 are already EOL'd. Java 11 is the latest LTS version.\r\n\r\nIt may be viable to stay on Java SDK 8 (Oracle or OpenJDK), but it would need to be something that we specifically suggest to contributors if OpenJDK 11 causes issues.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/comments/470403724/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Splaktar","id":3506071,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MDYwNzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3506071?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Splaktar","html_url":"https://github.com/Splaktar","followers_url":"https://api.gith